* {{IPA|en|/ˈsɒɾi/|a=Wales}}
* {{rhymes|en|ɒɹi|s=2}}

===Adjective===
{{en-adj|er}}

# Of a [[person]], [[regretful]] or [[apologetic]] for one's [[action]]s.
#: {{syn|en|apologetic|compunctious|contrite|penitent|regretful|remorseful|repentant|Thesaurus:regretful|Thesaurus:remorseful}}
#: {{ux|en|I am '''sorry''' I stepped on your toes. It was an accident.}}
# {{senseid|en|saddened}} Of a [[person]], [[grieved]] or [[saddened]], especially by the [[loss]] of something or someone.
#: {{syn|en|heavy-hearted|melancholy|mournful|Thesaurus:sad}}
#: {{ux|en|I feel '''sorry''' for you, about your exam results.}}
#: {{ux|en|The President was '''sorry''' to hear that the Ambassador was leaving.}}
# Poor, [[pitiful]]ly [[sad]] or [[regrettable]].
#: {{syn|en|pathetic|pitiable|Thesaurus:pitiful}}
#: {{ux|en|The storm left his garden in a '''sorry''' state.}}
#* {{quote-book|en|year=1948|author={{w|Truman Capote}}|title=Other Voices, Other Rooms|section=Part One, 1|passage=... often the only movement on the landscape is winter smoke winding out the chimney of some '''sorry'''-looking farmhouse ...}}
# [[pathetic#Adjective|Pathetic]]; [[contemptible|contemptibly]] [[inadequate]].
#: {{syn|en|deficient|insufficient|Thesaurus:inadequate}}
#: {{ux|en|Bob is a '''sorry''' excuse for a football player.}}
#* {{RQ:Guardian|author=David Smith|title=Failure to launch: Twitter glitches deal double blow to Elon Musk and Ron DeSantis|date=2023-05-25|url=https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-elon-musk-twitter-campaign-launch-glitch|passage=The '''sorry''' experience did little to suggest that Musk knows how to run a social media platform or that DeSantis is capable of governing a global superpower armed with nuclear weapons.|archiveurl=https://web.archive.org/web/20230810051150/https://www.theguardian.com/us-news/2023/may/24/ron-desantis-elon-musk-twitter-campaign-launch-glitch}}

